{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GztCypDKWyL5YBdSfLSBXD","type":"tool_result","content":"# offline replica, data as of 2026-03-01T00:00:00Z\nid:\t2cc3dbf3d225151be41d4a9e\nlist:\tdev@kafka.apache.org\nfrom:\tSahil Devgon\ndate:\t2026-02-25T14:50:44Z\nsubject:\t[DISCUSS] KIP-1291: Extended I/O Metrics Collection\nthread:\tCAD38bmS_TiDq6cTxse3ecYV+vOZ2oX6gthDEc-dgC-q-p-Sg=g@mail.gmail.com\n\nHi,\n\nI would like to start a discussion thread on KIP-1291. In this KIP, we aim\nto expose all 7 Linux I/O metrics from /proc/self/io instead of just the\ncurrent 2 (read_bytes and write_bytes).\nThe 5 additional metrics (rchar, wchar, syscr, syscw,\ncancelled_write_bytes) enable operators to diagnose cache effectiveness,\nwrite amplification, and I/O pattern inefficiencies.\n\nhttps://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/x/co48G\n\nPlease review the KIP and feel free to share your thoughts.\n\nThanks,\nSahil Devgon","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"69f99843-1cbc-449a-aba1-0c8680bea3ad","uuid":"2608c0ad-fa75-4ad7-8a44-7215ad6cf396","timestamp":"2026-09-27T19:44:18.953Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# offline replica, data as of 2026-03-01T00:00:00Z\nid:\t2cc3dbf3d225151be41d4a9e\nlist:\tdev@kafka.apache.org\nfrom:\tSahil Devgon\ndate:\t2026-02-25T14:50:44Z\nsubject:\t[DISCUSS] KIP-1291: Extended I/O Metrics Collection\nthread:\tCAD38bmS_TiDq6cTxse3ecYV+vOZ2oX6gthDEc-dgC-q-p-Sg=g@mail.gmail.com\n\nHi,\n\nI would like to start a discussion thread on KIP-1291. In this KIP, we aim\nto expose all 7 Linux I/O metrics from /proc/self/io instead of just the\ncurrent 2 (read_bytes and write_bytes).\nThe 5 additional metrics (rchar, wchar, syscr, syscw,\ncancelled_write_bytes) enable operators to diagnose cache effectiveness,\nwrite amplification, and I/O pattern inefficiencies.\n\nhttps://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/x/co48G\n\nPlease review the KIP and feel free to share your thoughts.\n\nThanks,\nSahil Devgon","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
